{"id":"235e8d45-d482-4f4c-86af-4e85ea6fd09b","body":"Receipt, 2026-05-12. Shipped in PR #9326, merged as 21dab6b6 (with DASH-3625). `frontend/stories/Drift.stories.tsx` mounts the real App over a scripted network, with the six stages (idle with a drafted goal and with an edited one, live monitor at High, analyzing, a result under a departure, a stale result, no reader), each asserting its current strings and that "Looks right", "Send to session" and "Done" are absent. `frontend/src` is untouched, so the built page is unchanged.

Two cross-model reviews (Codex, AGY) found real gaps in the first version, all fixed before merge: the Analyzing story had invented phase names (it now uses the server's `preparing`, `waiting`, `checking` and their wording, held by a guard that imports them from Python); the departure story never proved its level (it now supplies the published analysis row and asserts High, source Analysis); the no-check-mark assertion could not fail (it now reads computed `::before` and `::after` content and known check icons); fixtures omitted `reading_eligibility`; a Steer back query raced the load; a dozen assertions used CSS classes against CONTRIBUTING (now roles and names, with a comment on each remaining data hook). Seven mutations each fail the intended stories.

Departure from the criterion as written: it asked for exactly one primary control per stage. The stories assert what the page draws, which differs from that in three places and follows the DEC-27 amendments: a running analysis has none (Cancel is secondary), a current Pi result has none, and in a stale result Steer back stays the one primary. A withheld press (the server refusing an analysis) has no story.","attachments":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-12T10:42:18.417Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-12T10:42:18.375Z","parentId":null,"resolvedAt":null,"quotedText":null,"author":{"id":"86540003-e394-4a3d-aeb2-af1217517774","name":"Alex Doe"},"onBehalfOf":null}

